1
00:00:00,930 --> 00:00:03,630
(Penny:)So, Amy, I've
been wondering,

2
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:06,370
(Penny:)are you and Sheldon going
to be sharing a room?

3
00:00:06,370 --> 00:00:08,270
(Amy:)No, we discussed it.

4
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:10,370
(Amy:)We decided we didn't want
to jeopardize our relationship

5
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:12,200
(Amy:)by getting to know
each other too well.

6
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:15,870
(Sheldon:)Indeed. Nothing sours
a friendship more

7
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:19,680
(Sheldon:)than over-familiarity
with someone's toilet routine.

8
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:21,380
(Leonard:)I can vouch for that.

9
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:23,720
(Penny:)Hey.
Not you, him.

10
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:25,150
(Penny:)Oh. Thanks.

11
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:28,720
(Leonard:)Although yours
was an eye-opener.

12
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,590
(Amy:)Don't worry, Penny.

13
00:00:31,590 --> 00:00:33,890
(Amy:)You're my plus-one.
You'll bunk with me.

14
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:36,230
(Amy:)And FYI, travel
makes me constipated,

15
00:00:36,230 --> 00:00:38,900
(Amy:)so I'm the ideal
hotel roommate.

16
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,270
(Penny:)Terrific.

17
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:43,700
(Penny:)Are we there yet?

18
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:48,040
(Bernadette:)I hope we get there in time
to see the keynote address.

19
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,440
(Howard:)Really? You want to see
the keynote?

20
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,580
Yeah, it sounds fun.

21
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:53,950
"Super bacteria:

22
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:57,350
global apocalypse or
exciting research opportunity?"

23
00:00:57,350 --> 00:01:00,890
(Howard:)Actually, I was thinking we
could go straight to the room

